              "function_response": null,
              "inline_data": null,
              "text": "The URL **`www.home.fedex.com/express`** is the internal intranet homepage specifically for **FedEx Express employees**. \n\nHere is what you need to know about accessing it:\n\n### 1. Network Restrictions (Why it won't load at home)\nThis website is hosted behind the FedEx corporate firewall. If you try to open this URL from a personal phone, a home internet connection, or outside of the FedEx network, you will get a **\"403 Forbidden\"** error, a connection timeout, or the page simply will not load.\n\n### 2. How to Access It\nTo open this page, you must be connected directly to the FedEx network. You can access it by:\n* Using a **work computer, terminal, or \"thin client\"** while on-site at a FedEx station, hub, or facility.\n* Connecting via an authorized, company-provided VPN/network if you are working remotely.\n\n### 3. How to Access Your Employee Tools From Home\nIf you are at home and need to check your schedule, view paystubs, or access HR tools, you cannot use the `home.fedex.com` address. Instead, you should use FedEx's external-facing employee systems:\n* **Okta / Purple ID:** You can log in externally by going to [purpleid.okta.com](https://purpleid.okta.com).\n* **Workday:** You can use the Workday app or website to view your profile, hours, and internal job postings. \n* **Blue Yonder / Dimensions:** If your station uses these timekeeping and scheduling tools, they are typically configured via Okta or may require setting up MFA (multi-factor authentication) while you are on-site before they can be accessed from a mobile device. \n\n*If you are having trouble logging in or need to set up your Purple ID/Okta account for the first time, you will need to do so from a computer inside a FedEx facility or contact your manager/local HR for assistance.*",
